      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-50946",
      ":question/problem": "If $\u2211_(n = 1)^(\u221e)(-1)^{n}a_{n}$ is divergent and $a_{n}$ is a positive, strictly decreasing sequence for all $n \\ge 1$, then which of the following statements *must* be true?\n\n1. $\u2211_(n = 1)^(\u221e)(-1)^{n}a_{n}$ is absolutely convergent.\n2. $lim_(n \u2192 \u221e)a_{n} = 0$.\n3. $\u2211_(n = 1)^(\u221e)b_{n}$ is divergent, where $a_{n} \\le b_{n}$ for all $n \\ge 1$."
