      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-50951",
      ":question/problem": "If $\u2211_(n = 1)^(\u221e)a_{n}$ is convergent and $a_{n}$ is a positive, strictly decreasing sequence for all $n \\ge 1$, then which of the following statements *must* be true?\n\n1. Given that $f(n) = a_{n}$ where $f(x)$ is continuous and strictly decreasing, then $\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{\u221e}f(x)dx = \u221e$.\n2. $\u2211_(n = 1)^(\u221e)(-1)^{n + 1}a_{n}$ is convergent.\n3. $lim_(n \u2192 \u221e) \\mid \\frac{a_{n + 1}}{a_{n}} \\mid > 1$."
